// Title: Microsoft Teams Sensitive File Access By Uncommon Applications
// Sigma ID: 65744385-8541-44a6-8630-ffc824d7d4cc
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @SerkinValery
// Date: 2024-07-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1528
// Description: Detects file access attempts to sensitive Microsoft teams files (leveldb, cookies) by an
//   uncommon process.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/microsoft-teams-stores-auth-tokens-as-cleartext-in-windows-linux-macs/
//   - https://www.vectra.ai/blog/undermining-microsoft-teams-security-by-mining-tokens
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_access/file_access_win_teams_sensitive_files.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FileName contains "\\Microsoft\\Teams\\Cookies" or FileName contains "\\Microsoft\\Teams\\Local Storage\\leveldb") and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\Microsoft\\Teams\\current\\Teams.exe"))
